window.docContents[104].resolve({"/Sub/#Type-Systems--Sub___-Subtyping--Concepts--The-Subtype-Relation--Structural-Rules":{"contents":"To start off, we impose two \"structural rules\" that are\nindependent of any particular type constructor: a rule of\ntransitivity, which says intuitively that, if σ is\nbetter (richer, safer) than υ and υ is better than τ,\nthen σ is better than τ...\n\n                              σ <: υ    υ <: τ\n                              ----------------                        (trans)\n                                   σ <: τ\n\n\n... and a rule of reflexivity, since certainly any type τ is\nas good as itself:\n\n                                   ------                              (refl)\n                                   τ <: τ\n\n\n","context":"Type Systems\u0009Sub: Subtyping\u0009Concepts\u0009The Subtype Relation","header":"8.1.4.1. Structural Rules","id":"/Sub/#Type-Systems--Sub___-Subtyping--Concepts--The-Subtype-Relation--Structural-Rules"}});